er from a claim.\012\012# Skill selection\012\012Existing mandatory skill triggers in these instructions and your skill index still apply first and unchanged.\012Before starting work, read this skill in full and follow it while you do this task; where it conflicts with these instructions, these instructions win.\012- Picked for this task: diagnostic-reasoning - read /Users/charlesabrooker/.treehouse/firstmate-60912a/30/firstmate/.agents/skills/diagnostic-reasoning/SKILL.md\012Picked by jev-1.14.0 through typesafe from this project's skills (fit 0.63); your skill index still applies for anything else this task needs.\012\012# Current no-mistakes intent contract\012This section supersedes every earlier brief instruction about constructing `--intent`, but not later clarifications actually supplied by the captain.\012Use everything under `## Captain intent authorized for --intent` through the end of this brief, including any nested subheadings but excluding that heading, plus any later words the captain actually supplied as `--intent`; never include Firstmate specification or other mixed Task content.\012Preserve those words without adding speaker labels or direct address.\012Firstmate-authored constraints, acceptance criteria, implementation details, decisions, and tradeoffs are specification, not captain intent.\012The Definition of done's rule that `--intent` must be self-sufficient still governs the string you pass: resolve any report, decision, or PR the intent below refers to into its substance rather than passing the pointer.\012\012## Captain intent authorized for --intent\012"fix the root cause behind this" and "the process enabling the creation of the orphans should be remediated."\012\012The text the ask points at: firstmate itself started a second herdr server for the same session. A firstmate helper starts a new server whenever a status check fails, even when the old server is still alive. The orphan was stopped by hand; one herdr server is left. The ask is